# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules for innsegl.dev (RM-058, #66; doc 05 §3).
#
# Order matters: the first matching rule wins.

# doc 05 §3 asks the root host to serve "a redirect to
# github.com/Raymalian/innsegl". 302 rather than 301 — a permanent redirect is
# cached by browsers forever and this project may not host its source in the
# same place for the rest of time.
/repo                    https://github.com/Raymalian/innsegl  302
/repo/*                  https://github.com/Raymalian/innsegl/:splat  302

# Every path under the module root answers with the module page, which carries
# the go-import tag. Status 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect: the go command
# reads the tag out of the body of THIS response.
#
# Without this rule, resolving innsegl.dev/innsegl/cmd/innsegl still works —
# the toolchain walks the path down to the module root — but it spends a 404
# per path element to get there. With it, a subpackage resolves in one request.
#
# `/innsegl` itself is deliberately not matched here. It is a static file
# (innsegl.html, served at /innsegl by Pages' clean URLs) and nothing may
# stand between the go command and it.
/innsegl/*               /innsegl  200
